  "term": "speciation",
  "definition": "Speciation is the identification and measurement of the different chemical forms in which a substance occurs within a sample. In this source, it refers to analyzing phosphorus in bird feces to determine which phosphorus forms are present and how much of each form contributes to ecological risk.",
